WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.660
Two cold solutions sit in a bath of ice.

2
00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:05.320
Pour one into the other.

3
00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:08.540
At once, a yellow-orange solid appears.

4
00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:14.120
Each of its molecules is two benzene rings,
joined by a pair of nitrogen atoms.

5
00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:17.600
Yet benzene on its own is
colourless, just like water.

6
00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:23.120
So why does joining two rings through nitrogen
give a solid with such a strong shade?

7
00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:27.720
In this mission, you'll make
benzenediazonium chloride from phenylamine,

8
00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:29.490
keeping it ice-cold.

9
00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:32.380
Then you'll couple it with
phenol to make an azo dye,

10
00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:35.960
and learn to read a dye's
shade like a chemist.

11
00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:40.830
Your mission: explain why two joined
benzene rings make an orange solid.